            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Yoneda+embedding"} (∞,1)-Yoneda embedding
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is locally presentable, then also the converse holds:
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is a locally presentable
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op} \to \infty Grpd
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable functor
              precisely if it preserves
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+in+a+quasi-category"} limits
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop. 5.5.2.2
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              We need to prove that a limit-preserving functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : C^{op} \to \infty Grpd
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is an accessible localization of a presheaf category.
            %p
              So consider first the case that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo =
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = PSh(D)
              %em is
              a presheaf category. Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mi op
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi j
                          %mi op
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi F
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f : D^{op} \stackrel{j^{op}}{\to} PSh(D)^{op} \stackrel{F}{\to} \infty Grpd
            %p
              for the precomposition of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              with the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Yoneda+embedding"} (∞,1)-Yoneda embedding
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ′
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F' := Hom_{C}(-,f) : PSh(D)^{op} \to \infty Grpd
            %p
              the functor represented by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %p
              We claim that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi F
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \simeq F'
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is represented by
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo ∘
                      %msup
                        %mi j
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \circ j^{op}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F'
              preserve limits (hence colimits as functors on
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(D)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              that it is sufficient to show that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo ∘
                      %msup
                        %mi j
                        %mi op
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi F
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ∘
                      %msup
                        %mi j
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \circ j^{op} \simeq F' \circ j^{op}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Yoneda+lemma"} (∞,1)-Yoneda lemma
            %p
              Now consider more generally the case that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} reflective sub-(∞,1)-category
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(D)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo :
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L : PSh(D) \to C
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              reflector. Since it respects all colimits, the composite
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∘
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi op
                    %mo :
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi L
                          %mi op
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi F
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F \circ L^{op} : PSh(D)^{op} \stackrel{L^{op}}{\to} C^{op} \stackrel{F}{\to} \infty Grpd
            %p
              respects all limits. By the above it is therefore represented by some object
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in PSh(D)
            %p
              By the general properties of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} reflective sub-(∞,1)-categories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is the full
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} sub-(∞,1)-category
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(D)
              on those objects that are
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              sends to equivalences. But
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo ∘
                      %msup
                        %mi L
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \circ L^{op}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo ∘
                      %msup
                        %mi L
                        %mi op
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \circ L^{op}|_{C}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              is equivalent to the identity, so that this is equivlent to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          %p This statement has the following important consequence:
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              A locally presentable
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              has all small
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+in+a+quasi-category"} limits
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop. 5.5.2.4
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              We may compute the limit after applying the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Yoneda+embedding"} (∞,1)-Yoneda embedding
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi PSh
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j : C \to PSh_{(\infty,1)}(c)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} full and faithful (∞,1)-functor
              it is sufficient to check that the limit computed in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)
              lands in the essential image of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+in+a+quasi-category"} limit in a quasi-category
            %p
              to check for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo →
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \to PSh(C)
              a diagram of limit-preserving functors that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi lim
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim_i F_i
              is a functor that commutes with all limits, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi J
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a : J \to C
              be a diagram and compute (verbatim as in ordinary category theory)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mi i
                            %msub
                              %mi F
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mi i
                            %msub
                              %mi F
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mi j
                            %msub
                              %mi F
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mi i
                            %msub
                              %mi F
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi lim
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mi i
                            %msub
                              %mi F
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi lim
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\lim_j (\lim_i F_i)(a_j)
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    \\lim_j (\lim_i F_i(a_j))
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    \\lim_i (\lim_j F_i(a_j))
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    \\lim_i F_i(\lim a_j)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    (\lim_i F_i)(\lim a_j)
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
          %h3#PresentedByCombinatorialSimplicialModelCategories
            As
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            By prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EquivalentCharacterizations"}
            locally presentable
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
            which are
            %em presented
            by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+simplicial+model+category"} combinatorial simplicial model category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            in that they are the full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicially+enriched+category"} simplicial subcategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo ∘
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\circ \hookrightarrow C
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bifibrant+objects"} bifibrant objects
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            (or, equivalently, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-category
            associated to this
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicially+enriched+category"} simplicially enriched category
          %p
            (See also at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%28CombModCat%29"} Ho(CombModCat)
          #QuillenEquivZigZag.num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              Under this presentation,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} equivalence of (∞,1)-categories
              between locally presentable
              = succeed "-categories" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zigzags"} zigzags
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalences"} Quillen equivalences
              between presenting
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+simplicial+model+category"} combinatorial simplicial model categories
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo ∘
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\circ
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mo ∘
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^\circ
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} equivalent as (∞,1)-categories
              precisely if they are connected by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zig-zag"} zig-zag
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+Quillen+adjunction"} simplicial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalences"} Quillen equivalences
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ←
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ←
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mi D
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C
                    \\stackrel{\leftarrow}{\to}
                    \\stackrel{\to}{\leftarrow}
                    \\stackrel{\leftarrow}{\to}
                    \\cdots
                    D.
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Lurie"} Lurie, remark A.3.7.7
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              Partly due to the fact that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model categories
              have been studied for a longer time – partly because they are simply more tractable than
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
              – many
              = succeed "-categories" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
            %p
              The canonical example is the presentation of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
              on an ordinary (1-categorical)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              by the simplicial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model category of simplicial presheaves
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p The basic example is:
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
              is locally presentable.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, example 5.5.1.8
            )
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              According to the discussion at
              %a{:href => "limit+in+a+quasi-category#Tensoring"} (∞,1)-colimit – Tensoring with an ∞-groupoid
              every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
              is the colimit over itself of the functor contant on the point, the terminal
              = succeed "-groupoid." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
          .num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              An
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              is precisely a locally presentable
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} localization
              functor also preserves finite limits.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              locally presentable
              = succeed "-categories," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
